# CODEOWNERS — structural enforcement of the product-review boundary.
#
# A PR that touches ANY owned path below REQUIRES @TomDevine11's review before merge, and
# therefore cannot auto-merge. A PR that touches NONE of these paths can auto-merge once CI
# is green. Pair with branch protection: "Require review from Code Owners" + "Require status
# checks" (see docs/autonomy/RUNNER.md).
#
# STRICT START (by design): all application code under /src/ is owned, so ANY change to app
# code is assumed capable of affecting the product and needs Tom's review — even an ostensibly
# "internal" src refactor. We start conservative and loosen later, once the autonomous system
# has demonstrably operated safely (e.g. by carving out genuinely output-neutral src areas).
#
# What can still merge autonomously today: PRs touching NO owned path — tests (/test),
# documentation, most build/tooling scripts, dependency bumps (package.json), root config,
# and .claude. That is where "internal, self-mergeable after CI" currently applies.

# All application code (games, components, utils, SEO config, and the generated game data).
/src/                           @TomDevine11
# Static assets, entry HTML, OG image service, prerender — user/search-facing output.
/public/                        @TomDevine11
/index.html                     @TomDevine11
/og-service/                    @TomDevine11
/scripts/prerender.mjs          @TomDevine11
# Production deploy config.
/render.yaml                    @TomDevine11
# CI + the system's own charter — never auto-edited by the loop.
/.github/                       @TomDevine11
/VISION.md                      @TomDevine11
/CLAUDE.md                      @TomDevine11
/docs/autonomy/LOOP.md          @TomDevine11
/docs/autonomy/RUNNER.md        @TomDevine11
/docs/autonomy/ci.workflow.yml  @TomDevine11
